cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this course, cite it as below and also cite the paper its economic model comes from."
type: software
title: "Computational Economics: Teaching Examples and Python Implementation"
authors:
  - family-names: Wei
    given-names: Zhongji
    website: "https://zhongjiwei.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/weizj99/computational-economics-mp"
url: "https://computational-economics.zhongjiwei.org"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Independent teaching examples for moment matching, a two-period oligopoly
  economy, estimation and CPU/GPU computing. The economic model is based on
  De Loecker, Eeckhout and Mongey (2026), Quantifying Market Power and Business
  Dynamism in the Macroeconomy, doi:10.21034/sr.688. The course rebuilds the
  model in Python and estimates it on the paper's data. It uses its own
  parameter values, so its results can differ from the paper's. It does not
  represent the views of the paper's authors. All errors are my own.
references:
  - type: report
    title: "Quantifying Market Power and Business Dynamism in the Macroeconomy"
    authors:
      - family-names: De Loecker
        given-names: Jan
      - family-names: Eeckhout
        given-names: Jan
      - family-names: Mongey
        given-names: Simon
    year: 2026
    collection-title: "Staff Report"
    number: "688"
    institution:
      name: "Federal Reserve Bank of Minneapolis"
    doi: "10.21034/sr.688"
